CON-15: KINWAVE: raise the inlet area only by what the inflow fills

kinwave_execute() sets the inlet area to the normal-flow area of the new
inflow at once. When that rise needs more water than the step supplies (an
abrupt inflow into an empty or nearly empty conduit), the continuity
equation has no root with aout >= 0, solveContinuity() clamps aout = 0
(return code -3) and the conduit is booked with water that never entered.
In that case, lower the inlet area to the value for which the equation holds
with aout = 0 (f(0) = C2 = 0), never below the previous inlet area. The
inlet area then grows over the following steps as the inflow fills it.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply CON-15_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/kinwave.c b/src/legacy/engine/kinwave.c
index abb00e0..a9be382 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/kinwave.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/kinwave.c
@@ -144,6 +144,12 @@ int kinwave_execute(int linkIndex, double* qinflow, double* qoutflow, double tSt
             report_writeErrorMsg(ERR_KINWAVE, Link[linkIndex].ID);
             return 1;
         }
+
+        // --- if the inflow cannot fill a rise in inlet area within this
+        //     step (no outflow solution), raise the inlet area only by what
+        //     the inflow fills, so that continuity still holds
+        if ( result == -3 && ain > a1 )
+            ain = MAX(a1, ain - C2 * WX / ((1.0 - WT) * dxdt));
         if ( result <= 0 ) result = 1;
 
         // --- compute normalized outlet flow from outlet area
